              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kvmcnitt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried the recipe out, but found it to be too bland for me. So I added salt, onion powder, garlic powder, chipotle powder, paprika and some red cayenne powder to spice things up a bit. I added the spices in about 1/8 - 1/4 teaspoon amounts and tried the adjustments on four triangles of bread until I got the taste I liked. (It then wasn't an asian dish anymore.)",
